<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('../partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../partials/header') %>

  <main id="main-content">

    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="hero__inner">
        <p class="hero__eyebrow">Seaford, East Sussex</p>
        <h1 id="hero-heading" class="hero__heading">Four habitats.<br>One coastline.</h1>
        <p class="hero__lead">
          From a sunlit coral reef to a trench where daylight never reaches, Blue Harbour
          brings four marine worlds together under one roof and works to protect
          the real ones beyond our doors.
        </p>
        <p class="hero__actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/zones">Explore the zones</a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/experiences">See what&rsquo;s on today</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="zones-intro" aria-labelledby="zones-heading">
      <div class="page">
        <h2 id="zones-heading">Our zones</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Each zone recreates a habitat as closely as we can manage, down to water
          temperature, lighting and the rhythm of the tide.
        </p>

        <ul class="zone-grid">
          <% zones.forEach(zone => { %>
            <li class="zone-card zone-card--<%= zone.slug %>">
              <div class="zone-card__media" role="presentation"></div>
              <div class="zone-card__body">
                <h3 class="zone-card__title">
                  <a href="/zones/<%= zone.slug %>"><%= zone.name %></a>
                </h3>
                <p class="zone-card__tagline"><%= zone.tagline %></p>
              </div>
            </li>
          <% }) %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="conservation" aria-labelledby="conservation-heading">
      <div class="page">
        <h2 id="conservation-heading">Why we do this</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          An aquarium earns its place by doing more than displaying animals. Most of ours
          were bred in human care rather than taken from the wild, and the work we do here
          feeds directly into conservation beyond the building.
        </p>

        <ul class="fact-list">
          <li class="fact">
            <p class="fact__figure">180+</p>
            <p class="fact__label">coral fragments grown in our propagation lab and shared with reef restoration projects each year</p>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <p class="fact__figure">3</p>
            <p class="fact__label">endangered freshwater species we breed as part of a European conservation programme</p>
          </li>
          <li class="fact">
            <p class="fact__figure">12</p>
            <p class="fact__label">beach cleans run with local volunteers each year, with findings recorded for the Marine Conservation Society</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sensory" aria-labelledby="sensory-heading">
      <div class="page">
        <h2 id="sensory-heading">Planning a quieter visit</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Aquariums can be loud, bright and crowded. Every Tuesday from 9am to 11am we run a
          sensory-friendly session with reduced lighting, no public announcements and lower
          background sound. Each zone page also lists what to expect underfoot, overhead and
          in the air, so you can decide what suits you before you arrive.
        </p>
        <p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/faq">Read our accessibility FAQ</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>